  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "botchan-s07-p0004",
      "source_en": "From that night, I became a boarder with Mr. and Mrs. Hagino. The thing that surprised me most was that so soon as the day following that on which I left Ikagin, the curio dealer, Noda, the Clown, went in and occupied the very room where I had been, with as undisturbed a face as if it were a matter of course. Indifferent as I am, I was amazed beyond measure at this act of brazenness. The world seemed to be composed solely of impostors and schemers who were ever trying to scheme against, and impose upon, one another. Disgusted at this, I got tired of the world; I began to curse life itself.",
